name: array-len-fold
prereqs: [none — param("slice", …, "@", …) comes straight from the
  parser's subscript lowering, which tags `${#arr[@]}`'s length read by
  keeping the `#` in the NAME slot]
invariant: param("slice", "#NAME", "@", "") folds to arrayLen(NAME)
  only when NAME is a plain identifier ([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*) and the
  length slot is a literal ""/absent. `${#arr[@]}` / `${#arr[*]}` is
  bash's element count of the list, and arrayLen is the contract's
  element-count node — a renaming, not a semantic change. Kept
  untouched: plain-name list reads (a whole-list, not a length), any
  non-"@" offset (a numeric offset is a substring OF THE COUNT,
  `${#arr:2}`), non-empty/non-literal lengths, the (k) annotation
  arity, and any name that is not "#" + plain identifier.
scope: offered to all (estree, c, go, java, perl, python, rust, sh,
  fish, zig, zsh, glsl)
updates: none (first offer)